The port's image configs pass e2fsdroid the file contexts at obj/base/security/selinux/file_contexts.bin, where
older OH releases built them. OH 7.0 builds them at obj/base/security/selinux_adapter/file_contexts.bin, and
mkextimage.py leaves out a contexts file that does not exist without a word, so the system, vendor and userdata
images had no SELinux labels (every file u:object_r:unlabeled:s0 once SELinux was on).

diff --git a/fajita/image_conf/system_image_conf.txt b/fajita/image_conf/system_image_conf.txt
index 437396e..e6cfb0c 100644
--- a/fajita/image_conf/system_image_conf.txt
+++ b/fajita/image_conf/system_image_conf.txt
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@
 2684354560
 --fs_type=ext4
 --dac_config ../../build/ohos/images/mkimage/dac.txt
---file_context obj/base/security/selinux/file_contexts.bin
+--file_context obj/base/security/selinux_adapter/file_contexts.bin
